From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:17:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 159/161] hjviewer: review fixes for the App Store lane (1.9.1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An iPhone reads where it came from first and on its own (deviceValue), so
a device info that fails no longer leaves an App Store install on
TestFlight's way.

The Runner target's OTHER_LDFLAGS drop the Photos framework as well: only
the photo picker needed it, file_picker builds without its media picker,
and nothing else in the app or its pods refers to it.

The desktop's About keeps upstream's "Website" link, which opens in the
system browser like the other two: taking it out was none of the 1.9.1
decisions. hjvLinkTakesScheme's comment says that phones register
hjviewer:// alone from 1.9.1.

A source test pins the About links of the desktop and the phones to
LaunchMode.externalApplication and ko.rs's "개인정보 처리방침".

The Play bundle no longer has CAMERA (qr_code_scanner brought it), so the
public repo's client-build.yml loses that line of PLAY_MANIFEST in the
same push.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
